sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant API as AuthController
    participant DB as refresh_tokens

    B->>API: POST /auth/login (email, password)
    API->>API: BCrypt check, 5 fails = 15 min block
    API->>DB: store sha256(refresh), expires in 7 days
    API-->>B: accessToken (JWT, 15 min) in JSON<br/>Set-Cookie circl_refresh (HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/api/v1/auth)
    B->>API: GET /me/activities, Authorization: Bearer access
    Note over B,API: 15 minutes later
    B->>API: GET /me/activities
    API-->>B: 401 token expired
    B->>API: POST /auth/refresh (cookie sent by the browser)
    API->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE by hash, revoke old row, insert new
    API-->>B: new access token + new refresh cookie
    B->>API: retry GET /me/activities
    Note over B,DB: a stolen OLD refresh token shows up later
    B->>API: POST /auth/refresh (old token)
    API->>DB: row is already revoked, so revoke ALL tokens of that user
    API-->>B: 401, everyone has to log in again
